==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
You have quite a bit of time to stall at the beginning: the peons do very little damage and you can save up a lot.

The trick in this stage is to trigger the Boss Wave with speedy units like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] so that they can force the burrow from the Dread Bore and Zory before your [[Zombie Killer]] units reach the base. This way, they'll be a part of the fight instead of stuck in front of the Zombies that are now wrecking your front line.

Plan your fight properly and keep the meatshields constant, and you shouldn't have too much trouble with the Dread Bore, even with his 400k health.

If the freeze effect from the Maawth gives you trouble, bring along an [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] in some capacity so that it's less of a burden on you. The Maawth can be annoying but you must be able to handle it and the Bore in order to win.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
You can farm for a very long time in this stage because there are a lot of peons to fill your pockets with. Stall tactics can work here because the peons seem to last forever.

The real fight starts when you hit the base but before then you'll at least want a healthy team of meatshields and a couple Alien DPS units (or an uber) to deal with Maawth on the forefront. His many freezes may make you consider knockback units if he gives you too much trouble.

Since you get 3 immediate burrows from Dread Bore, Zory, and Zuche you may want to consider bringing the Holy Blast Cannon upgrade if you have it. If not, a perfectly timed Cat Cannon can be a big help. Incase you're worried about that, try the regular strategy instead.

Save most of your Zombie Killer units for after the boss wave. Then just let loose with as much as you can afford so that you can knock out the Zombies that make it through your front line. Spawn as many meatshields as possible during this time to protect from the fast attacking Zombies or you will lose hard and fast.

With proper timing, excellent meatshielding and good placement of units before the enemy base reaches 99% you should be able to beat this. If you're still struggling after a few attempts, go back and collect as many treasures as you can from Into the Future and try again when you're stronger. This level is a bit harder than most because of the surge of damage from the 3 hard hitting Zombies.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The one Maawth isn't too hard at the start so you can get up to level 3 cat wallet. The main issue here are The Thrillerz and making sure they don't get early access passes to damage your base with their double burrow and full hp revive.

Once you have all 3 Maawths you might struggle a little bit, especially with LeMurr coming out to support them with weakens. Because there are going to be a handful of Alien enemies this round, you'll definitely want your anti-Alien Cats with freeze, weaken or extra damage. You will likely end up with at least 5 LeMurrs stacked up but at least they're only Single Target and their range is low. Proper meatshielding will keep them at bay.

Dread Bore is a huge threat as always so Zombie Killers and Zombie CC like knockback, freeze, slow or weaken is a big help. Zomboe does its job of being annoying too so cheaper Zombie Killer units are recommended.

As usual, try to prevent Dread Bore from burrowing at all with your Cat Cannon if you can time it right (or just use Holy Blast). This will help the fight stay in one area. If not, the Dread Bore may burrow past your cats and destroy the base or your ubers in seconds. Saving a heavy-hitting Zombie Killer or unit with knockback can truly be a life saver here.

If the massive amount if Aliens or the high health Zombies give you a lot of trouble then you will want more treasures for sure before returning to attempt this map when it next appears.

